  "question": {
    "text": "If a spring has time period T, and is cut into n equal parts, then the time period of each part will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{T} \\sqrt{\\mathrm{n}}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{T} / \\sqrt{\\mathrm{n}}$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{nT}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{T}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Spring constant becomes $n$ times for each piece. $T=2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{k}}$\n$$\n\\frac{T_1}{T_2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{n K}}{K} \\text { or } T_2=T / \\sqrt{n}\n$$"
  }
}